\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MARCH 21, 2007\r\rMayor Washburn called the meeting to order at 7:43 p.m. in the City Council Chambers of City Hall, 26135 Mureau Road, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Washburn, Mayor pro Tem Bozajian, Councilmembers Groveman, Maurer, Wolfson.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Colantuono, Coroalles, Parker, Rubin, Steller, Tamuri, Yalda.\r\rThe Pledge of Allegiance was led by Patty Coroalles.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT\r\r Karyn Foley, Calabasas, expressed her congratulations to the newly re-elected Councilmembers and to the incoming Mayor and Mayor pro Tem. Nidia Lota, spoke regarding Councilmember Groveman�s 2006 Assembly campaign.\r\r\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015ELECTION 2007\r\r1. Adoption of Resolution No. 2007-1069, declaring the results of the March 6, 2007 General Municipal Election.\r\rGwen Peirce, Assistant City Clerk, presented the staff report and read the certified results.\r\rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Councilmember Groveman, to adopt Resolution No. 2007-1069, declaring the results of the March 6, 2007 General Municipal Election. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\r2. Administering of the Oath of Office to Councilmembers-Elect.\r\rThe Honorable Richard G. Kolostian administered the Oath of Office to Councilmember Dennis Washburn and Councilmember Barry Groveman.\r\rComments by Members of the City Council.\r\r Councilmember Groveman expressed his appreciation to the residents, City Council and staff of the City. Mayor Washburn reserved his comments for later in the meeting.\r\rCOUNCIL REORGANIZATION\r\rPresentations to outgoing Mayor\r\rOutgoing Mayor Dennis Washburn received special recognition from Cynthia Scott, representing Los Angeles County Supervisor Zev Yaroslavsky, Senator Sheila Kuehl and Assemblymember Julia Brownley; Stephanie Warren, representing the Calabasas Chamber of Commerce; Cindy Iser and Pat Schulz, representing the Las Virgenes Unified School District; and Mayor Stuart Siegel, representing the City Council and residents of the City of Hidden Hills. Mayor pro Tem Bozajian presented a special plaque to Mayor Washburn on behalf of the City. Councilmember Wolfson, Councilmember Maurer and Councilmember Groveman congratulated the newly re-elected Councilmembers and expressed their appreciation for Mayor Washburn�s dedicated service and leadership.\r\r\r\r\rOutgoing Mayor�s remarks\r\rOutgoing Mayor Washburn thanked City staff, City residents and Councilmembers for their support and highlighted the accomplishments of the City over the previous year.\r\r\rElection of Mayor and Mayor pro Tem\r\rCouncilmember Groveman moved, seconded by Councilmember Wolfson, to appoint James R. Bozajian as Mayor and Mary Sue Maurer as Mayor pro Tempore. MOTION CARRIED 5/0.\r\rOath of Office to Mayor and Mayor pro Tem\r\rThe Honorable Stephen Pfahler, Los Angeles Superior Court Judge, administered the Oath of Office to newly appointed Mayor James R. Bozajian and Mayor pro Tem Mary Sue Maurer.\r\rComments by Mayor\r\rMayor Bozajian expressed his appreciation to the City Council, City staff, Commissioners and residents for their work in the City and to his family and friends for their attendance. He outlined his goals for the upcoming year.\r\rADJOURN\r\r The City Council adjourned at 8:22 p.m.\r\r\r\r______________________________\rGwen Peirce, CMC\rAssistant City Clerk\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\u0003\r\r\u0004\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0013PAGE \u0014- 2 -\u0015\r03/21/07\r\rA copy of the City Council agenda packet is available for review at City Hall and the Calabasas Library.\r\rThe City of Calabasas, in complying with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), request individuals who require special accommodations to access, attend and/or participate in the City meeting due to disability, to please contact the City Clerk�s Office, (818) 878-4225, at least one business day prior to the scheduled meeting to insure that we may assist you.\r\r\r\r\r\r\r\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0006\u0000\u0000\u0001\b\u0000\u0000\u0015\b\u0000\u0000\u0016\b\u0000\u0000q\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000�\b\u0000\u0000\u001a \u0000\u0000\u001b \u0000\u0000$ \u0000\u0000K \u0000\u0000L \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000� \u0000\u0000\u000e\n\u0000\u0000\u0010\n\u0000\u0000���Ǹ�����